values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123923","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123923.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123923.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123912\r\nYou can now edit the color without the color picker closing. It also updates the texture live as it should.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nThis could be seen as a hacky fix, but it's by far the least hacky fix I could think of. Other ideas involved\r\n- Removing `notify_property_list_changed` from `ImageTexture`'s `set_image` and `update` methods, but this would break if people have added custom inspector plugins. This also doesn't cover the similar issue that ArrayMesh has in the same configuration.\r\n- Trying to use the regular `emit_changed` call instead of the \"preview\" direct set that https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/88690 introduced (that was also the cause of the issue this closes). However, problem with using `emit_changed` is that it gets commited to the undo log, which we don't want. So in this case we would need to run `emit_changed` without triggering undo, which I tried but found difficult/even hackier.\r\n\r\nThis is my first PR and is done as part of a CS course where we were asked to contribute to an open source project. I've thought about getting to know the Godot codebase for a long time so this was the perfect opportunity for me!\r\n\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123923/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}